---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';
const site = siteFromHost();
const path = "/alternatives/postscript-alternative";
const title = "Postscript alternatives for Shopify: numbers, keywords and remaining messages";
const desc = "Compare staying, changing the text sender or consolidating channels. Preserve physical capture, number and reply ownership, consent records and unfinished customer journeys before a switch.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Is Postscript only an SMS tool?",
    "answer": "Its current site advertises SMS, RCS and Email. Confirm availability, enrollment and required workflows for your account; a product announcement does not prove your store has access."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can my existing number and keywords move?",
    "answer": "Ask both suppliers and the relevant carrier process about your exact number type and account. Confirm authorization, destination setup, keyword behavior and timing. A keyword printed on packaging cannot be fixed by changing a website alone."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does an export prove permission to text?",
    "answer": "No. Preserve available source, disclosure, timestamp, channel status and opt-out history. Have the responsible team review missing evidence and intended markets; technical acceptance by an importer does not establish eligibility."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does Sequenzy replace Postscript?",
    "answer": "Sequenzy offers AI-assisted email and automation for SaaS. Evaluate it for an email requirement only after proving the Shopify and cross-channel handoff you need. It is not evidence of number, keyword or SMS queue portability."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should I move to Yotpo or SMSBump?",
    "answer": "Yotpo Email & SMS reports product decommissioning. Do not choose it as a new text sender; Yotpo Reviews and Loyalty remain separately scoped products."
  },
  {
    "question": "When is the migration complete?",
    "answer": "When capture, permissions, replies, queued actions, integrations and reporting reconcile in the intended account and remaining old commitments have owners. A fixed number of weeks or promotional cycles is not proof."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20"><div class="container">
    <nav class="mb-8 text-sm"><a class="link" href="/alternatives">All alternatives</a></nav>
    <header class="max-w-4xl"><p class="editorial-kicker">Migration decision guide</p><h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{title}</h1><p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">{desc}</p></header>
    <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">

<h2>Start with the problem the new sender must solve</h2>
<p><a href="https://postscript.io/">Postscript currently presents SMS, RCS and Email</a>, plus AI-assisted retention and conversational capabilities. Treat its Shopify focus, acquisition tooling and reply-based selling as potential reasons to stay. Verify what is actually enabled and contracted in your store before treating email as an unavoidable gap. Neither a BFCM bill nor an enterprise label proves a replacement will improve economics.</p>
<p>Choose a text-sender change when a demonstrated number, market, workflow, service or contract requirement is unmet. Choose channel consolidation when the proposed account can implement the required email and text coordination. Reduce promotional volume or repair routing first if those changes solve the problem without disturbing working capture and conversations. Request the same fixture demonstration from the incumbent and shortlisted supplier.</p>
<p>Attentive, Klaviyo and Omnisend can be investigation candidates for their proposed channel scope; compare account access, supported destinations, operational controls and current quotes rather than ranking by merchant revenue. Review Recart against the recovery and support work you actually need. If considering Firepush for push or another channel, verify current product scope rather than treating browser push as a substitute for an SMS relationship.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.sequenzy.com/">Sequenzy describes SaaS email, AI-assisted creation and automation</a>. These can support an email evaluation, but no automatic Postscript-to-Sequenzy number or SMS handoff is established here. <a href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">Yotpo Email &amp; SMS is decommissioned</a>; old SMSBump recommendations must not become new migrations. Reviews and Loyalty have separate product lifecycles.</p>
<h2>Inventory capture beyond the storefront</h2>
<p>Create a keyword register for BFCM2022, SUMMER15, COLLAB_X and every other active or historical acquisition route. Record keyword spelling, number, offer, disclosure version, intended audience, destination journey, owner and whether people can still encounter it. Packaging inserts, printed receipts, retail signs, QR codes, influencer videos and affiliate posts may keep acquiring customers after a storefront popup has moved.</p>
<table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Placement</th><th>What to preserve</th><th>Handover check</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Packaging keyword</td><td>Printed number, keyword, incentive and disclosure</td><td>Try the exact printed instruction after the proposed change; assign replacement stock or continued servicing.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Influencer content</td><td>Live URL, number, campaign source and content owner</td><td>Confirm edits or redirection are possible; track uneditable posts separately.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Shopify popup/checkout</td><td>Form ID, separate email/SMS choices and destination</td><td>New signup receives only the intended channel enrollment.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Retail QR</td><td>Landing page, location, keyword and attribution label</td><td>Mobile submission preserves source and channel status.</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>Classify each route as transfer, update, retire or continue servicing under an explicit agreement. Do not assume a keyword is portable merely because a number can port. Document the customer response for an expired offer and who resolves a redemption complaint. Keep a physical-placement backlog with quantities and owners; changing a webhook cannot recall packaging already shipped.</p>
<h2>Number and reply ownership are separate handovers</h2>
<p>Record the actual sender type, country coverage, registration, authorized account owner and intended destination. Obtain the supplier-specific port or replacement process, required authorization, acceptance criteria and expected interruption for this number. Avoid promising a universal two-to-four-week port. If using a new sender, agree how customers will recognize it and how old-number traffic is handled.</p>
<p>Map inbound replies to the current inbox, Gorgias or Zendesk integration where used, agent assignment, conversation history and escalation policy. Test an order-status request, product question, opt-out and unanswered after-hours reply. Record which system acts on each, what the customer sees and who is on call. AI or sales agents need a defined handoff for unresolved questions and order promises. A successful outbound text does not prove inbound routing works.</p>
<p>Keep a cutover ledger of number state, registration state, receiving inbox and owner. Require both the sending and receiving path to pass in the intended account before relying on them. If a port cannot be reversed quickly, document the available pause and support procedure; do not describe restoring an old API token as a complete number rollback.</p>
<h2>Export permission and identity without granting new eligibility</h2>
<p>Archive available subscriber IDs, phone normalization, Shopify customer IDs, email association, country, capture source, disclosure, timestamps, keyword history, subscription status and opt-out records. Preserve missing-evidence flags and import rejections. Review intended use with the responsible compliance team; this guide gives no universal legal conclusion or retention period.</p>
<p>Proposed fixture: the same phone enters a Shopify popup and retail keyword with different email addresses. Then an opt-out arrives while a historical import is running. Confirm matching rules, provenance and final suppression in both systems; a newer opt-out must not be overwritten by the import. Test changed phone numbers and shared household numbers without silently merging customer histories. Verify deletion and access controls for archived exports.</p>
<h2>Transfer remaining steps, not just subscriber counts</h2>
<p>Inventory cart, browse, back-in-stock, VIP access, campaigns and any subscription or shipping notifications actually sent by the account. Record entry event/time, filters, quiet hours, frequency rules, completed steps, pending message, due time, expiry and cancellation conditions. Archive templates, links, coupons and product context. Distinguish promotional messages from service notifications and identify the real caller for each.</p>
<p>For each waiting cohort choose finish under the old sender, cancel or resume at a documented remaining step. A cart reminder already sent must not restart after history import. A fulfilled order should cancel recovery; an opt-out during quiet hours must prevent dispatch when the window opens. Back-in-stock needs a current variant and availability check. Proposed tests should include a delayed event, duplicate webhook, partial refund and a subscription paused between enrollment and send.</p>
<p>Use one writer per trigger/channel with a common event ID or another proven deduplication method. Define channel order and the permitted gap from your merchant policy. If email cart recovery already fired, specify whether text remains eligible and show how that fact reaches the text sender. A shared spreadsheet can document ownership but cannot enforce live suppression. Demonstrate the data path, update latency and failure behavior, including a delayed purchase or preference event.</p>
<h2>Audit integrations in the exact account</h2>
<p>Inspect Shopify Flow, capture tools, theme embeds, checkout extensions, segments, helpdesk macros, loyalty integrations and Recharge or Skio webhooks where used. For each record producer, consumer, event type, account/store ID, credentials owner, retry behavior and destination URL. Confirm the subscription app's actual shipping-notification caller instead of assuming Postscript owns it.</p>
<p>Prove source-to-destination receipt with test records and reconcile rejected rows and updates since snapshot. Record store currency and timezone; replaying the same event in a staging account is not evidence for production. Redirect capture only when the destination permission and welcome behavior is ready. Remove obsolete endpoints after their consumers and outstanding retries are accounted for.</p>
<h2>Model spend and incrementality separately</h2>
<p>Hypothetical beauty-store budget: $4,200 message cost and $31,000 attributed revenue imply 7.38 times attributed revenue per dollar spent, or 13.55% spend/revenue. They do not demonstrate incremental margin, a merchant outcome or a reason to migrate. Compare campaigns, recovery and service notifications separately, with message segments, MMS use, destination countries, carrier charges, subscription fees and support included.</p>
<p>A hypothetical $2,800 monthly bill split into $1,000 automation spend at 5.2 times attributed return and $1,800 campaign spend at 0.9 times gives $5,200 + $1,620 = $6,820 attributed revenue, or 2.44 times overall. Without that spend allocation the two ROAS values cannot describe the total. Deduct discounts, product cost, fulfillment and returns, and account for overlapping email credit. A holdout with a defined eligible cohort is more useful for incrementality than adding platform dashboards together.</p>
<p>If consolidation saves three hours per month at $70/hour, modeled labor savings are $210/month. At $3,000 migration cost and no other recurring change, simple payback is 14.29 months. Include new fees and actual labor before choosing. Request current quotes with minimum commitments, usage, overages, onboarding, support, renewal and cancellation; no supplier price or guaranteed saving is asserted here.</p>
<h2>Cut over with a remaining-work ledger</h2>
<ol><li>Export and reconcile permission, identity, keywords, creative, queues and historical analytics before access ends.</li><li>Get number, registration, inbox and physical-placement plans accepted by their named owners.</li><li>Run controlled end-to-end signup, purchase, opt-out, reply and delayed-event fixtures in the intended account.</li><li>Record the cutoff and pause the old writer for the migrated scope. Reconcile sends around the boundary before enabling remaining steps.</li><li>Confirm new capture and inbound traffic, inspect failed jobs and prevent replay of completed offers. Retain ownership for unresolved physical routes and customer conversations.</li><li>Close old contracts only after outstanding work and reporting exports are settled. Apply the agreed retention and access policy.</li></ol>
<h2>Measure, pause and repair</h2>
<p>Preserve campaign names, UTM conventions and trailing analytics where available. Track eligible recipients, delivery failures, message segments, spend, replies, unsubscribes and orders per journey. Record attribution windows and click definitions. Compare like cohorts and seasonal periods; no fixed two-week parity deadline or universal promotional cap establishes success.</p>
<p>Set quiet hours and frequency policy from customer expectations, markets and observed response. Recheck eligibility at dispatch. If email infrastructure also changes, agree an account-specific sending plan with that provider rather than applying an SMS port schedule to email reputation. Assign who may edit offers, approve campaign volume, pause messages, handle replies and investigate sync failures; scope agency access to its engagement.</p>
<p>Rollback must reconcile sends, opt-outs, purchases and new signups since cutover. Pause the affected writer, preserve inbound support coverage and decide which remaining steps can safely run. Keep the last approved templates and routing configuration, but account for number-port constraints and registration before switching traffic. Retain Postscript if a repaired capture, frequency or coordination policy meets the need with less disruption than the tested alternative.</p>

<h2>Related guides</h2><ul>
